    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by the high-upside pairing of **Yordan Alvarez** (81.17) and **Trea Turner** (76.90). **Yordan Alvarez** remains the premier play against Yesavage; his elite xwOBA of .448 provides a massive ceiling, and he avoids the negative platoon splits that weigh down several other lineup spots. Meanwhile, **Trea Turner** and **Christian Yelich** (74.33) headline our attack against Lowder. Both benefit significantly from favorable #1 lineup spots and advantageous platoon matchups, with **Christian Yelich** seeing a substantial 13% boost from his dynamic platoon profile. **Kyle Schwarber** (71.24) also earns a premium start; despite a modest BvP flag, his ability to capitalize on the 4.65 xERA of Mikolas and his high-xwOBA profile solidify his status as a core component of today\u2019s offensive strategy.\n\nEfficiency in our stolen base pursuit drives the decision to start **Caleb Durbin** (69.13), who benefits from a slow-delivering opposing pitcher that bolsters his SB probability to 90%. Conversely, the most difficult decision of the morning involves **Casey Schmitt** (45.53), who narrowly missed the cut for the final utility spot. While **Casey Schmitt** offered a solid boost from projected wind conditions, the optimizer ultimately favored the superior base projection and dynamic platoon ceiling of **Nelson Velazquez** (51.34). We are monitoring the status of **Chase Meidroth** (48.36) closely; his matchup against Bibee carries a 32% rain risk, and any delay or postponement would necessitate an immediate pivot to our bench depth. We remain cautious with **Dillon Dingler** (57.22) and **Junior Caminero** (59.32), both of whom are projected as marginal starts due to specific platoon disadvantages, but they retain their spots as the lineup lacks superior alternatives for their respective positions today.",
